From: Adriel Santos <adriel.turox@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mpd: unwind a failed root PD start

q6_wcss_start() leaves everything it set up behind when it fails. On the
authenticate-and-reset error path it returns without unpreparing, and on
the start timeout it returns having neither shut the peripheral back down
nor unprepared. The peripheral is then left authenticated-and-reset in
TZ with no matching qcom_scm_pas_shutdown(), and the qcom_q6v5 context
still reads as prepared - running == true and the handover IRQ still
enabled, which is where the "Unbalanced enable for IRQ" warning on the
next attempt comes from.

Every later start therefore begins from the state the previous failure
left, so a restart that fails once fails identically forever, and the
repetition says nothing about the hardware.

qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c, the driver that replaced this one upstream, routes
every error path in wcss_sec_start() through a single unprepare label.
Do the same here, and shut the peripheral down again on the timeout so
the next authenticate starts from a clean slate.

While here, take the start timeout from 5 to 10 seconds, matching the
vendor driver.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel.turox@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -134,13 +134,25 @@
 	ret = qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset(desc->pasid);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(wcss->dev, "wcss_reset failed\n");
-		return ret;
+		goto unprepare;
 	}
 
-	ret = qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start(&wcss->q6, 5 * HZ);
-	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
-		dev_err(wcss->dev, "start timed out\n");
+	ret = qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start(&wcss->q6, 10 * HZ);
+	if (ret) {
+		if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
+			dev_err(wcss->dev, "start timed out\n");
+		/*
+		 * Undo the authenticate-and-reset, or the peripheral stays
+		 * held in TZ and every later attempt inherits this failure.
+		 */
+		qcom_scm_pas_shutdown(desc->pasid);
+		goto unprepare;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 
+unprepare:
+	qcom_q6v5_unprepare(&wcss->q6);
 	return ret;
 }
 
